  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Information Management and Institutional Strengthening on Migration for the Implementation of the Project for the Integral Development Plan for Central America</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to generate reliable information for evidence-based decision-making and to sensitize extension service providers (professionals who provide local agricultural technical advice to small producers), municipal technical units, and organizational leaders about those factors that motivate irregular migration, the risks, effects, and their approach to improve the care of returned and transit migrants in communities in San Marcos and Huehuetenango. The activities to be developed will be carried out within the framework of the Comprehensive Development Plan project implemented by the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO). The project is divided into two components: 1. Available and up-to-date information for evidence-based decision-making and 2. Raising awareness and discussion on migration: risks and challenges of irregular migration.</narrative>
  </description>
